`Vampire/Logic.lean` is VampLean, copied rather than depended on, and it is the library
Vampire's own generated Lean files import: one tactic per preprocessing inference rule
over the propositional and quantifier equivalences those rules need.

    VampLean — https://github.com/vprover/vamplean
    Part of the Vampire project, https://github.com/vprover
    Copied from revision 5a62658.

That repository carries no licence file or per-file headers of its own; it is used here
as part of Vampire, whose licence is at https://vprover.github.io/license.html. The only
change is that the declarations are in `namespace Vampire` instead of at the root, so
that a file can import this package and Mathlib at once — upstream declares about a
dozen names Mathlib also declares, and two modules declaring one name collide at the
import.

